  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Plotting the graph with given data we have,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9551faae-7bef-4bb2-b424-06c621bb12f9-image.png\" style=\"width: 255px; height: 180px;\" /></p><p>We know that, in any parabola, the length of the latus rectum&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and perpendicular distance from vertex to the directrix&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Therefore, the&nbsp;length of the latus rectum&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p>",
